    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615">

                <pb facs="0861" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">150.071 Control/175</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Western
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">of a Conversation With the Swedish Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Böstrom</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-15">March 15, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Swedish Minister called this morning to inquire about the prospects of
                    passage of the King-Dies Seaman’s Bill. He renewed the protests which his
                    Government had made in previous years, and which, he said, applied with equal,
                    if not greater, force today.</p>
                <p>I told him of the steps taken by the Department to bring to the attention of the
                    Senate Committee the opinions both of the Secretary of State and of foreign
                    countries, and also read him some excerpts from the hearings of 1932.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierrepont Moffat</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
